# Google OAuth clients for Drive sync (docs/13). Copy to .env and fill in.
#
# Desktop (macOS/Windows/Linux): create a "Desktop" OAuth client in Google Cloud
# Console with the Drive API enabled and the consent screen published "In
# production" (Testing mode expires refresh tokens after 7 days). Until these are
# set, Settings > Sync shows "Google client not configured" and disables sign-in.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# iOS: create a separate "iOS" type OAuth client (Application type: iOS, bundle
# id: com.xinyuan.readingpartner). It has NO client secret. Its id looks like
# 1234567890-abc.apps.googleusercontent.com. Two places must agree:
#   1) Set VITE_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID below (the frontend reads it at build time).
#   2) Put the reversed client id into src-tauri/tauri.conf.json under
#      plugins.deep-link.mobile[0].scheme, already set for this repo's client.
#      Reversed form: com.googleusercontent.apps.1234567890-abc (drop the
#      ".apps.googleusercontent.com" suffix, prepend com.googleusercontent.apps.).
#      This registers the Info.plist URL scheme at iOS build time; it cannot come
#      from this env var. See docs/18-iOS-Google登录.md.
VITE_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=

# Android: nothing reads this yet — selectAuthFlow() has no android branch, so
# Settings > Sync says "Google client not configured" on Android whatever is set
# here, and the CI APK build injects no VITE_GOOGLE_* at all. The variable is
# named in advance because whichever OAuth route is chosen (docs/23) needs a
# separate client: an "Android" type client (package name
# com.xinyuan.readingpartner) has NO client secret but does require the SIGNING
# CERTIFICATE'S SHA-1 — the release keystore the APK is signed with (`keytool
# -list -v -keystore <file> -alias <alias>`) — and Google disables its custom
# URI scheme redirect by default for clients created after 2023-10-02. As on
# iOS, the reversed client id would also have to go into src-tauri/
# tauri.conf.json under plugins.deep-link.mobile[].scheme, which is what
# generates the Android intent-filter at build time; it cannot come from an env
# var. See docs/23-Android落地调研.md.
VITE_GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID=

# --- iOS sideload (scripts/sideload-ios.py; local dev only, never committed) ---
# The Apple ID that signs the app onto a USB-connected device. Only these
# credentials touch Apple's servers; a 2FA code is asked for occasionally and
# typed interactively. With 2FA on, use an app-specific password.
# See docs/19-iOS侧载安装.md.
#
# Two accounts can coexist: the free one is the default (7-day profile, 3 apps),
# and `--dev` uses the Developer Program one (1-year profile). Their team IDs
# differ, so iOS will not install one over the other — deleting the device copy
# first is unavoidable, and it takes on-device data with it.
SIDELOAD_APPLE_ID=
SIDELOAD_APPLE_PASSWORD=
SIDELOAD_DEV_APPLE_ID=
SIDELOAD_DEV_APPLE_PASSWORD=
SIDELOAD_SIDELOADER_BIN=
# Optional: a local ipa path. Omit to auto-fetch the latest CI build via gh.
SIDELOAD_IPA=
